From 5cf84f3eda244f0a30684c2b323a5489edd9cb1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Schaller <cschalle@redhat.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:57:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] media: i2c: imx471: Raise the analogue gain limit to the
 sensor maximum

The analogue gain of this sensor follows the SMIA form

	gain = (m0 * code + c0) / (m1 * code + c1)

with m0 = 0, c0 = 1024, m1 = -1, c1 = 1024, that is

	gain = 1024 / (1024 - code)

IMX471_ANA_GAIN_MAX is 800, which caps analogue gain at 1024 / 224 =
4.57x. Code 960 gives 16x, the sensor maximum, so the driver is giving
up 1.8 stops of sensitivity.

This is not theoretical: on a Lenovo ThinkPad X1 Carbon Gen 14 the
software ISP saturates both exposure and analogue gain and still
underexposes an ordinary indoor scene by around 3.8 stops.

Measured on that machine, comparing the median signal of the green
channels against the formula, with the black level removed:

	code	predicted	measured
	   0	  1.000x	  1.000x
	 512	  2.000x	  2.000x
	 800	  4.571x	  4.571x
	 960	 16.000x	 16.071x

Raising the limit therefore buys a measured 3.48x over the previous
ceiling, against 3.50x predicted.

Signed-off-by: Christian Schaller <cschalle@redhat.com>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/imx471.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/imx471.c b/drivers/media/i2c/imx471.c
index 2db1b05b5..bfffafa85 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/imx471.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/imx471.c
@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@
 /* Analog gain control */
 #define IMX471_REG_ANALOG_GAIN			CCI_REG16(0x0204)
 #define IMX471_ANA_GAIN_MIN			0
-#define IMX471_ANA_GAIN_MAX			800
+#define IMX471_ANA_GAIN_MAX			960
 #define IMX471_ANA_GAIN_STEP			1
 #define IMX471_ANA_GAIN_DEFAULT			0
 
